{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fix implemented and pushed as Gerrit change 2122 (commit 2e2dc69c123). Plan-review PASSED and was signed (ironically the attestation initially failed to persist under tracker churn — bug a83f-6348's exact starvation — and was recovered via rebar sign-review). RED->GREEN held-out tests added to tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign_heldout.py: transient store-read-failure retries then signs (calls==2); persistent failure exhausts MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS into a structured retry-after-repair refusal; deterministic malformed-reference refuses on the first attempt. make lint, make typecheck, complexity ratchet (new=0 increased=0) all green. Note: tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign.py::test_resign_routes_through_pin_collecting_sign_path times out locally on UNMODIFIED HEAD too (materialize_tickets against the real shared tracker with repo_root=None) — environmental, not introduced by this change. caused_by analysis: git log -L on the resign baseline-collect region -> introduced by 94e605a29d2 (ticket 5967-4476-7f9f-442d, 'Add phased plan-review attestations'), same origin ec1e attributed its half to; ec1e's fix scoped itself to sign_manifest and filed this ticket as discovered_from rather than shipping past an obligation, so attribution goes to resign's originating ticket: caused_by=5967-4476-7f9f-442d, class=plan_defect (same asymmetric terminal handling of a normal concurrency transient, from the same commit)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787434142575357001,"uuid":"97b12744-2b69-4a7e-a2e4-d0e66100f540"}